# Everything Docker would otherwise upload as build context.
#
# The two entries that matter are .venv and .env. The virtualenv is 4.7 GB --
# 4.0 GB of it a CUDA torch build that is wrong for the server anyway -- and
# .env holds the real Anthropic key, the Supabase keys, and the ingest worker's
# password. Without this file both are copied into the build context, the secret
# ones land in an image layer, and `docker history` reads them straight back
# out. Secrets reach the container through the environment at RUN time, never
# through a COPY.

.venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Built on the server with its own VITE_API_BASE_URL, so a local build would be
# baked with the wrong API origin. Vite inlines env vars at build time.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Not part of the running application.
agentic-rag-plan/
backend/evaluation/
supabase/
.git/
.github/
*.md
!README.md

# Local tooling noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
